# (#126) INTERROGATIVES ARE CENSUS ENTRIES. `prev of p`, `where is p` and
# `what is q at L` all NAME a binding, so p and q keep their env slot and
# their boundness answers come from the env exactly as before; `m` is named
# by no read and compiles to a plain C static with its own boundness bit.
#
# The observer-snapshot kinds (where/why/how) and the tape-reading kinds
# (what/who/when/prev) go into the census TOGETHER rather than being split
# by kind: boundness (bound_bit_of, and the `prev of` env-membership arm)
# and the observed-storage arms key on the SAME name, so a split would let
# the two disagree about where the binding lives -- which is invariant 14's
# storage-regime trap, and the way the first draft of this gate died.
p is 1.0
q is 1.0
m is 0
loop while m < 4:
    p is p * 2.0
    q is q * 3.0
    m is m + 1
print of f"p {p} q {q} m {m}"
print of f"p-report {report of p}"
print of f"prev-p {prev of p}"
print of f"where-p-at {where is p at 16}"
print of f"why-p-at {why is p at 16}"
print of f"what-q-at {what is q at 17}"
